graphics and escape sequences: known limits
  - lib/cl-libsixel and lib/kitty-graphics (and ecma48, kitty-keyboard, terminal-osc)
    should eventually be extracted into their own projects
  - ghostty reports only scrolls that grow its scrollback; region and alternate-screen
    scrolls are inferred from the screen.  libghostty-vt's tracked grid refs follow
    index scrolls but not RI/IL/DL/SD, and a discarded row's ref lands ambiguously on
    a live row, so they cannot replace the inference
  - SDL2 draws every negative-z image below the cell backgrounds (one cached grid
    texture; a middle layer needs a second texture with alpha)
  - ltk draws no underlines and reports key presses only
  - underline styles and colors: libvterm has no underline color or dotted/dashed,
    3bst only plain underlines
